\section{Agreement over a sample}
\label{sec:agreement-samples}

Every number above describes the records the two screeners screened,
and nothing more.  Those records are seldom a sample of anything
Scholar can name: a second screener checks the classifier's discards,
or the papers the author found doubtful, and the agreement over them
says nothing about the records nobody checked twice.  So the text gives
no interval for them, as the sampler gives none for a census
(\cref{sec:llm-sample} in the LLM review module).

A review sample drawn with [[llm sample]] is different: its papers were
drawn at random from a named population, and the share of them on which
the two screeners agree is a binomial proportion, agreeing records out
of those drawn.  For it the text gives the 95\,\% modified Wilson
interval of Brown, Cai and DasGupta, which the sample's own report
already uses, for the reasons given there ([[modified_wilson_interval]],
\cref{sec:llm-sample} in the LLM review module); it is the one interval
the sources read back.  It covers the observed agreement only.

Which papers count follows the sample's own report
([[sample_reports]]), so that the two never describe different sets: a
sample is stored in every session it pooled, and its papers are looked
up by id in each; papers of sessions not given count as not found,
unless their files can still be read ([[pooled_sample_sessions]]); and
a paper reset to pending after the draw ([[reset_since_draw]]) no
longer holds the decision the sample drew, so it is left out and
counted apart.  A stratified sample is stored as one sample per
confidence band, tied by a group id (\cref{sec:llm-sample-bands} in the
LLM review module); asked for the group, the text gives one block per
band and no line for the whole, since no estimator for a proportion of
agreeing records over the bands was read.  A band taken whole (a
census) gets no interval, as in the sample's report.

The interval assumes that the agreement was observed on the drawn
papers.  When some of them lack a verdict from one of the two
screeners, or, for the category questions, a category, the records
with both are the part some selection left, not a random sample, so the
interval is withheld and the text says how many are missing.  The
sample's own report does otherwise: it gives an interval over its
reviewed part and says that it covers only that part.  There the
missing papers wait for the one reviewer the sample was drawn for.
Here a paper lacks a verdict because a screener chose not to screen
it, or gave no category, and either choice may go with how hard the
paper was to judge, which is what agreement measures; so the papers
left would not stand for the drawn ones, and no caveat would make the
interval theirs.  Papers
reset since the draw or not found are counted apart and do not withhold
it, as in the sample's own report.

<<agreement samples>>=
@dataclass
class SampleBand:
    """The papers of one stored sample (or band) and their verdicts."""

    sample_id: str
    criteria: dict
    drawn_at: str
    size: int
    records: list = field(default_factory=list)
    reset_since_draw: int = 0
    not_found: int = 0

    @property
    def census(self) -> bool:
        """Whether the band took its whole population."""
        return bool(self.criteria.get("census"))

    @property
    def counted(self) -> int:
        """The drawn papers found and not reset since the draw."""
        return len(self.records)
@

[[sample_bands]] gathers the bands of the sample [[sample_id]] (a
sample's id or a stratified sample's group id) from [[sessions]], which
the caller has already completed with the pooled ones.  A sample stored
twice in one session is read once there, as in the sample's report.

<<agreement samples>>=
def _belongs(sample, sample_id: str) -> bool:
    stratum = sample.criteria.get("stratum")
    return sample.sample_id == sample_id or (
        isinstance(stratum, dict) and stratum.get("group") == sample_id
    )


def sample_bands(sessions, sample_id: str) -> list[SampleBand]:
    """The bands of the stored sample `sample_id` over `sessions`.

    One band for a plain sample, one per confidence band for the group
    id of a stratified one, in band order; empty if no session holds it.
    """
    from scholar.llm_review import reset_since_draw

    bands: dict[str, SampleBand] = {}
    for session in sessions:
        current = {get_paper_id(d.paper): d for d in session.decisions}
        seen: set[str] = set()
        for sample in session.llm_samples:
            if not _belongs(sample, sample_id) or sample.sample_id in seen:
                continue
            seen.add(sample.sample_id)
            band = bands.setdefault(sample.sample_id, SampleBand(
                sample.sample_id, dict(sample.criteria), sample.drawn_at,
                sample.size,
            ))
            for entry in sample.papers:
                decision = current.get(entry.get("paper_id"))
                if decision is None:
                    band.not_found += 1
                elif reset_since_draw(decision, sample.drawn_at):
                    band.reset_since_draw += 1
                else:
                    band.records.append(screener_verdicts(decision))
    for band in bands.values():
        found = band.counted + band.not_found + band.reset_since_draw
        band.not_found += max(0, band.size - found)
    return sorted(
        bands.values(),
        key=lambda b: (b.criteria.get("stratum") or {}).get("band", 0),
    )
@

[[band_agreement]] counts a pair's table over a band and adds the
interval when it applies; [[interval_withheld]] says why it does not,
in words the text prints.

<<agreement samples>>=
def interval_withheld(table: AgreementTable, band: SampleBand) -> str | None:
    """Why `table` over `band` has no interval, or None when it has one."""
    if band.census:
        return "a census of its population, no interval"
    missing = band.counted - table.n
    if missing:
        return (
            f"no interval: {missing} of the {band.counted} sampled papers "
            "lack a verdict or a category of one of the two screeners"
        )
    if not table.n:
        return "no interval: no sampled paper screened by both"
    return None


def band_agreement(
    band: SampleBand, a: Screener, b: Screener, question: str = "status"
) -> AgreementTable:
    """`screening_agreement` over `band`, with the interval if it applies."""
    from dataclasses import replace

    from scholar.llm_review import modified_wilson_interval

    table = screening_agreement(band.records, a, b, question)
    if interval_withheld(table, band) is not None:
        return table
    return replace(
        table, interval=modified_wilson_interval(table.agreeing, table.n)
    )
@

