The shared session's table is symmetric: its two off-diagonal cells
are equal and both indices are zero, so a swap of the cells or of the
indices would read the same.  The next session is not: an agent
screens seven decisions a human confirmed after a classifier proposed
them, kept by both in one, by the agent alone in two and by neither in
four.  Its observed agreement is $5/7$, its positive agreement
$2/(2 + 2 + 0) = 0.50$, its negative agreement $8/(8 + 2) = 0.80$, its
prevalence index $(1 - 4)/7 = -0.43$, its bias index $(2 - 0)/7 =
0.29$ and its kappa $(35/49 - 27/49)/(22/49) = 0.36$, with $P_e =
\tfrac37\cdot\tfrac17 + \tfrac47\cdot\tfrac67 = 27/49$.  The second
screener is the human-confirmed decision, which the caption names so.
A human some of whose verdicts are confirmations is named with their
count.

