\paragraph{Nothing added without screenings.}
A session without screenings must get every document it got before
the double screen existed.  An earlier version of this test pinned the
digests of those documents as written by the code before this section
(\texttt{b05c49e}).  That pinned far more than the property: the first
unrelated change to the report (a sentence about doubtful abstracts,
issue~\#287) changed a digest and failed the test, though the double
screen still added nothing.  The property is about this section's own
contribution, so the test now states it that way: each of the three
functions through which the documents read the double screen
([[double_screening_sentences]] for the report, [[summary_rows]] for the
synthesis, [[audit_screening_sentence]] for the caption) gives nothing
for such a session, and each document is the same text as the one
produced with those functions replaced by ones that give nothing.  The
CSV has no column for screenings, which the test checks on its header.

